        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Darmera, Melissa\n- Concepts: plant taxonomy, native range, growth habit\n\nFacts:\n- Darmera is a slowly spreading rhizomatous perennial native to mountain streamsides in woodland in the western United States, from southwestern Oregon to northwestern California.\n- Darmera grows to 2 m tall and 1 m wide.\n- Melissa is a genus of perennial herbs in the Lamiaceae.\n- Melissa is native to Europe and Asia but is cultivated and naturalized in many other places.",
